From ac2364e0e2660ec524f69c46d66d459e8a8b41f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rodney Pantonial <rodneypantonial@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 09:11:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Inventory cleanup: skip the name lookup for objects
 without an inventory

CheckInventories looked up the localized catalog name of every object in the world before CheckInventory returned early for the ones without an inventory. The name is only used in log lines, and with lots of store content each lookup searches many string tables, so this lookup was most of Overwatch's nightly 'Cleanup Inventory' time (~400-500 ms in one frame in our profiles). Same objects checked, same results.
---
 NRaas/Helpers/Inventories.cs | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/NRaas/Helpers/Inventories.cs b/NRaas/Helpers/Inventories.cs
index 499c0c9..20f4b4b 100644
--- a/NRaas/Helpers/Inventories.cs
+++ b/NRaas/Helpers/Inventories.cs
@@ -177,6 +177,9 @@ namespace NRaas.CommonSpace.Helpers
         {
             foreach (GameObject parent in Sims3.Gameplay.Queries.GetObjects<GameObject>())
             {
+                // Skips the localized name lookup for the many objects without an inventory
+                if (parent.Inventory == null) continue;
+
                 CheckInventory(log, debugLog, GetName(parent), parent.Inventory, checkDestroyed);
             }
 
From d8f171795a2a2196185b05f6d49df5bc1fba38fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rodney Pantonial <rodneypantonial@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 09:12:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Inventory cleanup: spread the nightly run over several
 frames

The nightly alarm runs CheckInventories with a sleep after every 25 inventories, so the work is split over many frames instead of one. The menu action still runs in one go. Objects destroyed while sleeping are skipped, and the household list is copied since it can change meanwhile. The old three-argument overload keeps its behaviour for the other mods sharing this helper.
---
