From a0157382ccdba982a5663699b1341e63bfd90a0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rodney Pantonial <rodneypantonial@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 09:14:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Nightly alarm: give each cleanup its own time

OnTimer ran every nightly cleanup in the same frame. With the new 'Set Alarm Spacing' setting (default 10 sim-minutes) each cleanup is scheduled as its own alarm task, spaced by that many sim-minutes from the alarm hour, so their costs no longer add up in one frame. Set it to 0 for the old all-at-once behaviour. Every cleanup keeps its own on/off setting and does the same work as before; with spacing, nightly notices show one by one instead of in one batch.

StaggeredCleanupVersion is a public marker for other mods (for example performance mods that spread these cleanups themselves) to detect this behaviour and stay out of the way.
